==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|proportional|ity}}, from {{der|en|la|proportionalitas}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɹəpɔɹʃəˈnæləti/|/pɹəpɔɹʃɪnˈælɪti/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-proportionality.ogg|a=Mid-Atlantic US}}
* {{rhymes|en|æləti|ælɪti|s2=6}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} the [[property]] of being [[proportional]]
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} the [[principle]] that [[government]] [[action]] ought to be proportional to the ends achieved (e.g. the [[military]] should not be deployed to stop petty vandalism)
# {{lb|en|countable}} the degree to which something is in [[proportion]]

